      "title": "Understanding Curves with a Compass",
      "explanation": "A curve drawn on paper using only a pencil and compass is called a circle. To draw a circle, fix the point of the compass at a specific location (the center) and move the pencil along the edge while keeping the distance constant. The shape formed is always a circle.",
